                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I'm giving this a positive review because I hope that Gen 42 still gets a cut when this game is sold.  I also love the aesthetic and it's nice to be able to play Hive in 3D with friends.  It's also pretty fun for beginners who will find the AI's higher difficulties challenging.  The current state of online matchmaking is pretty bad, though.  I think it technically works, but I haven't been able to actually play against someone yet and there are few players left anyway.  Don't buy this hoping to play online against strangers.  There are other free options out there that actually work.\r\n\r\nIt's nice to be able to play against friends locally or online, though.  I've had fun for the hours I've played this game despite the game being outdated.  You definitely don't need to buy this to play, but I find it charming and I've had enough fun with it to justify the price.",
